  "body": "The conjecture did not misread the rule. The rule as written says: “The object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one, else the last top-level object in the text.” The code’s `_FENCE` pattern is `re.compile('```(?:json|JSON)?\\s*(.*?)```', re.DOTALL)`, so it only treats ```json, ```JSON, or a bare ``` as a fence. A ```yaml fence is not matched, so the fenced pool is empty for Reply 1, and the last top-level object `{\"a\":2}` is returned. Thus the rule as written and the code part company. A next conjecture should try a ```json or bare fence, or a ```yaml fence with no later top-level object, to see whether the fence pool is used at all; it should avoid repeating the ```yaml-plus-later-object example, because the code’s fence regex explicitly excludes ```yaml and the later object will always win as the last top-level candidate."
